{#
  Clients, a slow marquee of real client logos.

  Replaces the four hand-typed names that stood here before. The band runs the
  full set continuously rather than showing four at a time, because the roster
  is the argument: a football club, a water utility, two pharmaceutical
  companies, an estate and a hospice is a wider spread than any static row of
  four can show.

  Behaviour (progressive enhancement): with no CSS animation, and for anyone
  who asks for reduced motion, the track stops and becomes a plain horizontal
  scroll list. Nothing here needs JavaScript, so there is no clients.js.

  The marquee runs on a duplicated set. The second copy is aria-hidden and
  carries empty alt text, so a screen reader is read the roster once, while the
  eye sees an unbroken loop. See clients.css for why the translate is exactly
  -50%.

  NOT lazy-loaded, deliberately. Every other image on the site is, and the same
  instinct here silently broke the band: lazy loading tests whether an image
  intersects the viewport, and the cells past the right-hand edge sit outside it
  inside a clipped, transformed track. The browser never re-tests them as the
  animation carries them in, so Amgen, IAC, Carel and DIS simply never loaded,
  and four cells ran empty forever. The whole set is 128KB and the two heavy
  PNGs have been cut to the size they actually display at, which is a cheaper
  price than a trust band that loses a third of its logos.

  Expects the `clients` global from _data/clients.js. Optional page overrides:
    clientsSurface  section modifier, defaults to section--light
    clientsTitle    the heading, HTML allowed, `em` gives the Playfair italic
    clientsId       unique id, only needed if two bands share a page
    clientsClass    extra class on the section. `clients--airy` is the service
                    page treatment: 10% larger marks, a slower loop, a centred
                    heading and more room above and below

  Light surfaces only. The marks are dark ink greyed down to 72%, so they need
  a pale ground to read against; dropped on the navy the row would vanish into
  it. clients.css has the long version.
#}
{% set cid = clientsId or "clients" %}
{% if clients and clients.length %}
<section class="section {{ clientsSurface or 'section--light' }} clients{{ ' ' + clientsClass if clientsClass }}"
         aria-labelledby="{{ cid }}-title">
  <div class="container">
    <h2 id="{{ cid }}-title" class="statement">
      {{ clientsTitle | safe if clientsTitle else "A few of the people <span class='em'>who rely on us.</span>" | safe }}
    </h2>
  </div>

  {# data-no-gloss: the track scrolls, so a term glossed in a logo label would
     be a tooltip that walks away from the pointer. See the gloss filter. #}
  <div class="clients__viewport" data-no-gloss>
    <ul class="clients__track" role="list">
      {% for c in clients %}
      <li class="clients__logo" style="--s: {{ c.scale }}">
        <img src="{{ ('/assets/logos/' + c.file) | v }}" alt="{{ c.name }}"
             width="{{ c.w }}" height="{{ c.h }}" decoding="async" draggable="false">
      </li>
      {% endfor %}
      {# The loop's second half. Hidden from assistive tech: same logos, and the
         roster should be announced once, not twice. #}
      {% for c in clients %}
      <li class="clients__logo" style="--s: {{ c.scale }}" aria-hidden="true">
        <img src="{{ ('/assets/logos/' + c.file) | v }}" alt=""
             width="{{ c.w }}" height="{{ c.h }}" decoding="async" draggable="false">
      </li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ul>
  </div>

  {% if 'clients--ruled' in (clientsClass or '') %}
  {# A closing hairline, for when the band is the first half of a pair and the
     section below continues the same argument on the same surface. Inside the
     container, so it lines up with the heading rather than running the full
     bleed the logos do. #}
  <div class="container"><div class="rule clients__rule"></div></div>
  {% endif %}
</section>
{% endif %}
